SUMMARY:The Longest Day: A Summer Solstice Workshop
DESCRIPTION:The solstice is the sun at its peak\, the longest day\, the fullest light. But it’s also a turning point. From here\, the dark begins its quiet return. It’s a moment of balance\, of honoring what is beofre it shifts. \nIn this one-hour workshop\, we’ll move through three phases: \nWe’ll move through the history and lore of the summer of the summer solstice\, drop into a guided meditation\, and make a botanical intention tray pressed with solar and lunar herbs. Yours to take home\, yours to keep on your altar\, a daily reminder of what you called in on the longest day. \nNo experience needed. All materials included.
URL:https://downtowndurham.com/event/the-longest-day-a-summer-solstice-workshop/
LOCATION:Fate & Folklore\, 123 Market Street\, Durham\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Classes & Workshops,Spiritual/Religious,Storytelling
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://downtowndurham.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/4.jpg
ORGANIZER;CN="Fate and Folklore":MAILTO:fateandfolkloredurham@gmail.com
GEO:35.9968012;-78.9021696
